SCOPE: Fix EI injection/parenteral path in injection_support.py + wiring. Product-agnostic. Do NOT touch OSD path or mass-based injection paths that already work. Reproduce approved TSR-VAS-09-00008 (all elements <30% PDE → PASS).

ROOT CAUSES (two, both must be fixed):

UI MDD + doses/day are collected but discarded — injection path hardcodes parse_injection_excel(raw, product_name, doses_per_day=1) and self-derives MDD from Excel (fails for units-dosed solutions → 0 rows / mdd=0).
Annexure "<30% of permitted" / ND ceilings are treated as measured values on the injection path → false exceedances (Pb 2002% vs approved 0.00). is_below_option1_qualitative not firing here.

FIX 1 — MDD as authoritative UI input with unit toggle. Add a unit selector beside MDD: mg or units. Wire the UI MDD value + unit into the injection backend (replace the hardcoded doses_per_day=1). MDD is authoritative — never re-derive it from Excel when provided.

FIX 2 — Volume-based dosing mode for solutions (new). When composition is per-mL (any row uses /mL), compute:

volume_per_day (mL) = MDD ÷ API_concentration_per_mL   [same unit as MDD toggle]
component_daily (g) = component_conc_mg_per_mL × volume_per_day ÷ 1000
total_product (g/day) = volume_per_day × density

If MDD unit = units and API row is in units/mL → divide directly (no potency needed).
If MDD unit = mg and API row is in mg/mL → divide directly.
Set calculation_model="volume_based", daily_intake_unit="mL/day" / grams via density.
Option 2a vs 2b: if total_product > 10 g/day → Option 2b (concentration-based summation), else 2a. (Approved: 731.5 g/day → 2b.)

FIX 3 — Dual-strength worst-case split (auto, no pop-up). When a cell carries multiple strengths (e.g. 0.2 units / 0.4 units), split on /, compute volume/day for each, and select the worst case = lowest API concentration → largest volume → highest excipient burden. Product-agnostic: fixed API dose ÷ lowest API conc = largest volume. (Approved uses 20u/720 mL → Dextrose 36 g, NOT 40u/360 mL.)

FIX 4 — Density: optional, post-parse pop-up, default 1.0. If density is present in Excel → use it. If absent → after Excel processing, pop a single optional field "Bulk density (g/mL)" (default 1.0, skippable). Warning-first, never hard-block. Only affects total grams / Option 2a-vs-2b threshold, not per-element concentrations.

FIX 5 — doses/day as FALLBACK only. Keep doses/day for true discrete-dose injections (fixed-volume vial × N/day). Priority: (a) volume-based mode if per-mL composition + MDD present → use it; (b) else fall back to per-unit mass × doses/day. Never use doses/day for a per-mL solution when MDD is available.

FIX 6 — ND / "<30% permitted" → ZERO on injection path (decisive). Apply existing is_below_option1_qualitative logic in the injection calc: any annexure element reported as "<30% of permitted concentration", "meets Option 1", "% of permitted" unit, or ND/BLD/BLQ → resolves to 0.0 µg/day, NOT the ceiling. This reproduces approved Total Daily Intake = 0.00 for all elements → PASS. This fix is independent of dose basis (0 × anything = 0) and is mandatory for a correct conclusion.

VALIDATION (must reproduce approved):

Input: MDD = 144 units (or 0.272 mg), Excel = per-mL, both strengths.
Expect: volume/day = 720 mL, Dextrose daily = 36 g, total = 731.5 g/day → Option 2b.
Expect: all elements Total Daily Intake = 0.00 µg/day (ND→zero) → all <30% PDE → PASS, no confirmatory testing.

REGRESSION GUARD: OSD (mg/tab), mass-based ratio injections (Medroxy), MDD-column injections (Aprepitant), mg/mL sheets → byte-identical output. Only the per-mL volume mode + MDD wiring + ND→zero on injection path are new.
